## 4. Authentication & RBAC (v3)

### 4.1 Updated AppUser Model (Shared Pydantic)

  # shared/models/user.py
  class UserRole(str, Enum):
      CANDIDATE   = "CANDIDATE"
      EMPLOYER    = "EMPLOYER"
      EXPERT      = "EXPERT"     # NEW
      EMPLOYEE    = "EMPLOYEE"   # NEW
      SUPER_ADMIN = "SUPER_ADMIN"

  class AppUser(BaseModel):
      id: str
      firebase_uid: str
      email: str
      primary_role: UserRole
      available_roles: list[UserRole]  # NEW: multi-role support
      display_name: str
      photo_url: Optional[str] = None
      is_active: bool = True

### 4.2 Auth Registration Flow

  POST /api/auth/register
  Body: { "firebase_token": "<idToken>", "requested_role": "CANDIDATE" }
  (EMPLOYEE and SUPER_ADMIN are granted by SUPER_ADMIN only — not self-service)

  Flow:
    1. verify_id_token(firebase_token) -> get firebase_uid, email
    2. Check if user exists in PostgreSQL
       YES: return existing user (idempotent)
    3. INSERT INTO users (firebase_uid, email, primary_role, available_roles)
       VALUES (..., requested_role, ARRAY[requested_role])
    4. Create empty profile in MongoDB
    5. Emit user.registered Kafka event
    6. Return AppUser JSON with available_roles[]

### 4.3 Multi-Role Grant (SUPER_ADMIN Only)

  PATCH /api/admin/users/{id}/roles
  Body: { "add_role": "EMPLOYER" }

  Flow:
    1. UPDATE users SET available_roles = array_append(available_roles, 'EMPLOYER')
    2. Invalidate Redis cache for this user
    3. Emit user.role.added Kafka event -> email notification to user
    4. Return updated AppUser

### 4.4 GET /auth/me Response Shape (Must Match FE AppUser Interface — camelCase)

  {
    "id": "uuid",
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "role": "CANDIDATE",
    "availableRoles": ["CANDIDATE", "EMPLOYER"],
